WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:07.480
<v Safi>I found a clump of jelly in the water. Each little ball has a dark centre. What is it?

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:18.109
<v Nuri>That’s a clump of common frog eggs. Each egg has a jelly coat. Draw what you see today in your notebook.

00:00:18.659 --> 00:00:26.417
<v Safi>I’ve drawn the eggs beside the reeds. If we come back, will we still see those little round shapes?

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:37.309
<v Safi>Days have passed. Today I can see tiny swimmers emerging from the eggs. Their tails swing from side to side.

00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:45.228
<v Nuri>Those are tadpoles. Early on, their tails help them swim, and their gills take in oxygen from the water.

00:00:49.078 --> 00:00:59.236
<v Safi>Several weeks later, I’m drawing one with a tail and hind legs. Do tadpoles grow legs before their tails disappear?

00:00:59.786 --> 00:01:09.395
<v Nuri>Yes. Compare it with your earlier drawing. Hind legs appear first, then front legs. For a while you can still see the tail.

00:01:12.495 --> 00:01:21.376
<v Safi>Today I can see all four legs, but the tail is shorter. It used to reach past the back legs. Now only a little is left.

00:01:21.926 --> 00:01:31.135
<v Nuri>As it grows, its body gradually absorbs the tail. The froglet starts coming into the shallow water at the edge.

00:01:34.235 --> 00:01:40.164
<v Nuri>If you find one with hind legs and a long tail, where would its picture go in your notebook?

00:01:43.364 --> 00:01:50.797
<v Safi>After the tadpole without legs and before the short-tailed froglet. We can look at the legs and the tail together.

00:01:53.897 --> 00:02:02.127
<v Safi>Here is a real adult common frog. Compare its back legs with my first drawing.

00:02:05.227 --> 00:02:13.383
<v Safi>I’ll take my drawings home. The eggs and tadpoles can stay in their pond. Thank Allah for creating these little lives.
